ory Co-op Programs Business Administration Co-op Program Optional Arts and Science Internship Work Experience Programs Optional Master of Public Relations Internship Co-op & Internship Important Dates Student Resources Student FAQs Hire a Student Co-op & WIL Employer Centre Important Dates for Employer Partners Employer Resources Employer FAQs Co-op Student of the Year Awards Co-op Employer of the Year Awards Inspiring Stories Co-op in the Business Administration Program: “Worth Every Single Minute” An Optimistic Perspective on Tourism and Hospitality after COVID-19 Another Year of Mount Co-op Student Excellence Recognizing the Many Contributions of Mount Co-op Employers in 2020 A Journey Less Travelled: BPR Grad-Turned-Entrepreneur of Local Vintage Shop, Florence’s Collection “It’s all about the experience” – Tourism grad pursues her passion of creating customized, sustainable travel experiences Full Circle: From Co-op Student to Co-op Supervisor Innovation, Flexibility and Confidence: Celebrating the Contributions of Mount Co-op Students in 2021 Celebrating the Mentorship of Mount Co-op Employers in 2021 Keeping Up with the Mount Co-op Office Jump into the challenge: tried and true advice from an international BPR student Beyond the Work Terms: What to Expect When Walking Across the Stage and Into the Workforce Go for the Gusto: A Tourism Alum Reflects on the Journey Back to MSVU Another Year of MSVU Co-op and Work Integrated Learning on the Books (Literally!) When a connection becomes a career: a BPR student’s journey to post-grad employment From student to supervisor: one student’s upward journey at Future Inns Hotel Introducing a new internship option for MSVU’s Master of Public Relations Students Bridging Worlds: A Mi’kmaw Student’s Journey Toward Leadership in Indigenous Tourism Investing in Experience: How WIL Is Shaping Canada’s Workforce Future Soaring to New Heights – Finding Confidence and Clarity through Internship Taking my Degree Down Under A Work Ter