      "description": "Careers at the Mount Home myMount / Email Moodle WebAdvisor Library Contact Us Home Search Hide Menu Future Students Academics Bachelor of Arts (BA) Aging Canadian Studies Chinese - Mandarin Communication Cultural Studies Economics English Family Science French History Library (courses) Mathematics Modern Languages Philosophy Political Studies Psychology Public Policy Religious Studies Sociology/Anthropology Spanish Women’s Studies Writing (minor) Bachelor of Science (BSc) Biology Chemistry Computer Science (courses) Mathematics Physics (minor) Psychology Statistics Professional Studies Applied Human Nutrition (BSc) Business Administration Child and Youth Study Information Technology Public Relations Tourism and Hospitality Faculty of Education Bachelor of Education Graduate Programs in Education -  Curriculum Studies - Educational Foundations - Educational Psychology - Elementary and Middle School Education - Literacy Education - Lifelong Learning - School Psychology - Teaching English to Speakers of Other Languages PhD in Educational Studies Doctor of Psychology (PsyD) Graduate Studies at the Mount Aging and Family Science Applied Human Nutrition Child and Youth Study Public Relations & Communication Education Women and Gender Studies Diploma & Certificates Library Online Learning Teaching and Learning Centre Experiential Learning Academic Calendars Co-operative Education & Work-Integrated Learning Centre Study Abroad See all Academic Programs Campus Life International Alumni & Donors Research About MSVU Home » About MSVU » Careers at the Mount Careers at the Mount Show Show Section Menu About MSVU Media Centre  |  News Event Calendar University Profile University Policies Tradition and History Financial Statements & Reports University Statistics and Reports Survey Highlights Enrolment Stats at a Glance Board of Governors Board Committees Board Policies Board Orientation Board of Governors' Manual Board Nominations Senate By-Laws and Terms of