 Indigenous Initiatives An apology and our commitment to Indigenous Peoples Indigenous Resource Hub/L’nuey Etl-Mawo’tumk L’nu Advisory Circle Faculty Resources People and Culture Equity, Diversity, Inclusion & Accessibility (EDIA) Faculty and Staff EDI MSVU Accessibility Plan EDIA Hub Strategic Enrolment Management (SEM) Plan MSVU Mascot Human Resources at MSVU At the Mount, you will find a dynamic, challenging and welcoming environment. Located on the Bedford Basin in Halifax, our campus offers beautifully landscaped grounds with spectacular views of the harbour. The Mount community is friendly and safe; we value diversity and acknowledge the richness of different cultures. We believe in social responsibility and making a difference in our community. The Human Resources team has much to offer you in navigating the workplace. We provide a comprehensive range of HR services including recruitment and selection, policy and guidelines, strategic and operational advice and support for health and wellbeing. You will find useful general information on this HR website, such as our Anti-Harassment and Discrimination Policy . As a Mount community member you will have access to the HR intranet that covers all phases of a career cycle, from orientation through to retirement. Contact the Human Resources team Human Resources Mission Facilitate a welcoming and respectful culture of highly knowledgeable and engaged staff and faculty focused on creating the best university experience for all members of the Mount community. This will be achieved through the design and implementation of progressive Human Resources policies and programs. Home 166 Bedford Highway , Halifax, Nova Scotia, B3M 2J6 MSVU is located on unceded ancestral Mi’kmaq territory. Social Media » Connect with MSVU Facebook X Instagram YouTube Social Media myMount/email Moodle Intranet WebAdvisor Media Centre Parking & Security Campus Map © 2026 MSVU Disclaimer Website Feedback Sitemap"
