      "description": "Employee Recognition & Appreciation Home myMount / Email Moodle WebAdvisor Library Contact Us Home Search Hide Menu Future Students Academics Bachelor of Arts (BA) Aging Canadian Studies Chinese - Mandarin Communication Cultural Studies Economics English Family Science French History Library (courses) Mathematics Modern Languages Philosophy Political Studies Psychology Public Policy Religious Studies Sociology/Anthropology Spanish Women’s Studies Writing (minor) Bachelor of Science (BSc) Biology Chemistry Computer Science (courses) Mathematics Physics (minor) Psychology Statistics Professional Studies Applied Human Nutrition (BSc) Business Administration Child and Youth Study Information Technology Public Relations Tourism and Hospitality Faculty of Education Bachelor of Education Graduate Programs in Education -  Curriculum Studies - Educational Foundations - Educational Psychology - Elementary and Middle School Education - Literacy Education - Lifelong Learning - School Psychology - Teaching English to Speakers of Other Languages PhD in Educational Studies Doctor of Psychology (PsyD) Graduate Studies at the Mount Aging and Family Science Applied Human Nutrition Child and Youth Study Public Relations & Communication Education Women and Gender Studies Diploma & Certificates Library Online Learning Teaching and Learning Centre Experiential Learning Academic Calendars Co-operative Education & Work-Integrated Learning Centre Study Abroad See all Academic Programs Campus Life International Alumni & Donors Research About MSVU Home » About MSVU » Careers at the Mount » Human Resources (HR) » Employee Recognition & Appreciation Employee Recognition & Appreciation Show Show Section Menu About MSVU Media Centre  |  News Event Calendar University Profile University Policies Tradition and History Financial Statements & Reports University Statistics and Reports Survey Highlights Enrolment Stats at a Glance Board of Governors Board Committees Board Policies Board Orientation Board of Governors' Manual Board Nominations Senate By-Laws and Terms of Reference Standing Committees Other Senate-Related Committees Policies Senate Award Honorary Degrees Senate Minutes Senate Agendas Items for Communication Freedom of Information and Protection of Privacy (FOIPOP) FOI - Freedom of Information POP - Protection of Privacy How can I protect my personal information? Privacy Impact Assessment Routine Access Policy FOIPOP - FAQ Freedom of Expression Statement Social Responsibility Quick Facts Strategic Plan Context Themes Transformative teaching and learning Research, scholarly work and professional activity Equity, diversity, inclusion and accessibility Truth and Reconciliation Community engagement A healthy and safe university campus for all Operational Excellence and Sustainability Process Environmental Scan Consultation Feedback Mid-point progress report Careers at the Mount Human Resources (HR) Faculty & Staff Relations FAQ - CUPE 3912 Strike Impacted Courses Strike Protocols Student Updates Collective Agreements Bargaining Archives Employee Recognition & Appreciation Contact HR Why Work at the Mount Current Openings Harassment and Discrimination Policies and Guidelines Managers and Professional Administrators (MPA) Leadership Team University Chancellor President and Vice-Chancellor Former Presidents Vice-President Academic and Provost Vice-President Administration Associate Vice-President University Relations Associate Vice-President Student Experience Associate Vice-President, Research Associate Vice-President of People and Culture Dean of Arts & Science Dean of Education Dean of Professional & Graduate Studies University Librarian President’s Fund – Special Projects Program Contact MSVU Social Media Channels Trauma-Informed language and interviewing Facilities Management The Freda Wales Trail MSVU E-Bike Rental Program Sustainability Initiatives Facilities Improvement Project The MSVU Community Garden About the Garden Workshops and Events at the Mount Community Garden Get Involved Contact Us Indigenous Initiatives An apology and our commitment to Indigenous Peoples Indigenous Resource Hub/L’nuey Etl-Mawo’tumk L’nu Advisory Circle Faculty Resources People and Culture Equity, Diversity, Inclusion & Accessibility (EDIA) Faculty and Staff EDI MSVU Accessibility Plan EDIA Hub Strategic Enrolment Management (SEM) Plan MSVU Mascot Our people are our foundation MSVU is shaped by our staff and faculty. Every day, you do meaningful work that makes a difference for those who work, live, and study on our campus. With a strong commitment to fostering equity, diversity, inclusion, and accessibility (EDIA) and social responsibility, many members of our community go above and beyond what is expected of them. We offer both informal and formal recognition programs to celebrate these efforts, with support from Human Resources. Informal Recognition Program: Giving Thanks A simple thank-you can go a long way. Whether someone offers help, shows kindness, or leads an important initiative, it matters to recognize their contributions. Thank You Cards You can share your appreciation with a handwritten “Thank You” card. These cards are: Free for employees Blank inside for personalized messages Designed to encourage peer-to-peer recognition Request your cards today by emailing thankyou@msvu.ca . Formal Recognition Programs Long Service Recognition Program Each year, the President hosts a luncheon and dinner to honour staff and faculty for their years of service. The event takes place on the first Tuesday of November and celebrates permanent employees who reach milestones such as: 5 years 10 years 15 years 20 years 25 years (and beyond) President’s Awards The President’s Awards recognize employees who make a significant impact on the MSVU and the wider community. There are two awards: President’s Award for Service to Mount Saint Vincent University Recognizes outstanding contributions to the University and progress toward its strategic plan. President’s Award for Volunteer Service to the Extended Community Recognizes meaningful volunteer work beyond the University. We encourage all members of the MSVU community to submit nominations. For details and nomination forms, visit the MSVU Intranet (login required) . Home 166 Bedford Highway , Halifax, Nova Scotia, B3M 2J6 MSVU is located on unceded ancestral Mi’kmaq territory. Social Media » Connect with MSVU Facebook X Instagram YouTube Social Media myMount/email Moodle Intranet WebAdvisor Media Centre Parking & Security Campus Map © 2026 MSVU Disclaimer Website Feedback Sitemap"
