nt Community Garden Get Involved Contact Us Indigenous Initiatives An apology and our commitment to Indigenous Peoples Indigenous Resource Hub/L’nuey Etl-Mawo’tumk L’nu Advisory Circle Faculty Resources People and Culture Equity, Diversity, Inclusion & Accessibility (EDIA) Faculty and Staff EDI MSVU Accessibility Plan EDIA Hub Strategic Enrolment Management (SEM) Plan MSVU Mascot Inspired by a strong tradition of social responsibility and an enduring commitment to the advancement of women, Mount Saint Vincent University promotes academic excellence and the pursuit of knowledge through scholarship and teaching of the highest quality. Recognized as a leader in flexible education, applied research, and a personalized approach to education, Mount Saint Vincent University (the Mount) is located on Canada’s East Coast in Halifax, Nova Scotia. The Mount sits on a beautiful wooded property overlooking a picturesque harbor. It is our blend of passion and individuality that attracts outstanding faculty, staff and students from around the world. Mount Saint Vincent University is seeking candidates for full-time faculty appointments for the positions listed below. Workload for tenure-track (probationary) faculty positions includes teaching, research, and collegial service. Workload for term faculty positions, senior administrative positions, and special research positions are in accordance with the posted position. Salary and benefits are in accordance with the specifics of the appointment and the requirements of the current Collective Agreement where applicable. All positions are subject to final budgetary approval. The following link will navigate away from the University’s website: Faculty Association Home Page Home 166 Bedford Highway , Halifax, Nova Scotia, B3M 2J6 MSVU is located on unceded ancestral Mi’kmaq territory. Social Media » Connect with MSVU Facebook X Instagram YouTube Social Media myMount/email Moodle Intranet WebAdvisor Media Centre Parking & Security Campus Map © 2026 MSVU Disclaimer Website Feedback Sitemap"
