of Governors' Manual Board Nominations Senate By-Laws and Terms of Reference Standing Committees Other Senate-Related Committees Policies Senate Award Honorary Degrees Senate Minutes Senate Agendas Items for Communication Freedom of Information and Protection of Privacy (FOIPOP) FOI - Freedom of Information POP - Protection of Privacy How can I protect my personal information? Privacy Impact Assessment Routine Access Policy FOIPOP - FAQ Freedom of Expression Statement Social Responsibility Quick Facts Strategic Plan Context Themes Transformative teaching and learning Research, scholarly work and professional activity Equity, diversity, inclusion and accessibility Truth and Reconciliation Community engagement A healthy and safe university campus for all Operational Excellence and Sustainability Process Environmental Scan Consultation Feedback Mid-point progress report Careers at the Mount Human Resources (HR) Faculty & Staff Relations FAQ - CUPE 3912 Strike Impacted Courses Strike Protocols Student Updates Collective Agreements Bargaining Archives Employee Recognition & Appreciation Contact HR Why Work at the Mount Current Openings Harassment and Discrimination Policies and Guidelines Managers and Professional Administrators (MPA) Leadership Team University Chancellor President and Vice-Chancellor Former Presidents Vice-President Academic and Provost Vice-President Administration Associate Vice-President University Relations Associate Vice-President Student Experience Associate Vice-President, Research Associate Vice-President of People and Culture Dean of Arts & Science Dean of Education Dean of Professional & Graduate Studies University Librarian President’s Fund – Special Projects Program Contact MSVU Social Media Channels Trauma-Informed language and interviewing Facilities Management The Freda Wales Trail MSVU E-Bike Rental Program Sustainability Initiatives Facilities Improvement Project The MSVU Community Garden About the Garden Workshops and Events at the Mount Community Garden Get Involved Contact Us Indigenous Initiatives An apology and our commitment to Indigenous Peoples Indigenous Resource Hub/L’nuey Etl-Mawo’tumk L’nu Advisory Circle Faculty Resources People and Culture Equity, Diversity, Inclusion & Accessibility (EDIA) Faculty and Staff EDI MSVU Accessibility Plan EDIA Hub Strategic Enrolment Management (SEM) Plan MSVU Mascot Inspired by a strong tradition of social responsibility and an enduring commitment to the advancement of women, Mount Saint Vincent University promotes academic excellence and the pursuit of knowledge through scholarship and teaching of the highest quality. Recognized as a leader in flexible education, applied research, and a personalized approach to education. The Mount sits on a beautiful wooded property overlooking a picturesque harbour. It is our blend of passion and individuality that attracts outstanding faculty, staff and students from around the world. Mount Saint Vincent University is seeking candidates for part-time faculty appointments for the positions listed below. Part-time faculty are contracted on a per-course basis in accordance with the Collective Agreement with CUPE local 3912: PT Faculty Collective Agreement . Remuneration is in accordance with the specifics of the appointment and the requirements of the Collective Agreement. All positions are subject to final budgetary approval and confirmation of enrollment. Mount Saint Vincent University is committed to the principles of employment equity and encourages applications from all qualified candidates including women, aboriginal persons, visible minorities and persons with disabilities. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, priority will be given to Canadians and permanent residents. PLEASE NOTE: part-time faculty positions are forwarded to CUPE local 3912. They are posted on the CUPE 3912 website and included in bulk notification emails. At all times, the posting on the Mount website is the official posting. Applicants are advised to consult the Mount website for complete information and application details. For information regarding Course Delivery Modes, please consult: https://www.msvu.ca/academics/online-learning/course-delivery-modes/ Home 166 Bedford Highway , Halifax, Nova Scotia, B3M 2J6 MSVU is located on unceded ancestral Mi’kmaq territory. Social Media » Connect with MSVU Facebook X Instagram YouTube Social Media myMount/email Moodle Intranet WebAdvisor Media Centre Parking & Security Campus Map © 2026 MSVU Disclaimer Website Feedback Sitemap"
